From: Ladislav Michl <ladis@triops.cz>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 09:45:54 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Makefile.am: build tbench_srv again

The switch to automake dropped the tbench server from the build, but
the sockio ("tbench") backend of dbench still needs it on the other
side of the connection. Build it again from the same sources as the
old hand-written Makefile did.
---
 Makefile.am | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/Makefile.am b/Makefile.am
index 0a335c1..c1e7f6b 100644
--- a/Makefile.am
+++ b/Makefile.am
@@ -1,9 +1,11 @@
 
-bin_PROGRAMS = dbench
+bin_PROGRAMS = dbench tbench_srv
 
 dbench_SOURCES = fileio.c util.c dbench.c child.c system.c snprintf.c sockio.c nfsio.c blockio.c libnfs-glue.c socklib.c \
 	linux_scsi.c libiscsi.c
 
+tbench_srv_SOURCES = tbench_srv.c socklib.c util.c
+
 LIBS += -lz
 
 if HAVE_LIBNFS
